---
import ServicePage from "@/components/ServicePage.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Button from "@/components/starwind/button";

const pageTitle = "Consulting";
const description =
  "Every team hits moments where the product feels slow, the architecture feels heavy, or the roadmap feels impossible to execute. I help teams cut through that complexity so they can move forward with clarity and confidence.";
---

<BaseLayout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
  <ServicePage title={pageTitle} description={description}>
    <h2>What I Do</h2>
    <p>
      My consulting work is hands‑on, collaborative, and focused on building
      systems that are fast, stable, and easy to work with. I diagnose the real
      issues behind performance, reliability, and delivery friction—guiding your
      team toward solutions that are clear, maintainable, and built to last.
    </p>
    <h3>Performance Optimization & Technical Diagnostics</h3>
    <p>
      Software applications slow down for all kinds of reasons: hidden
      bottlenecks, architectural drift, or small decisions that compound over
      time. I help teams uncover the real causes behind performance issues and
      fix them with clarity and precision. You get faster load times, smoother
      interactions, and a system that feels reliable instead of fragile.
    </p>
    <p>
      Typical outcomes:
      <ul>
        <li><b>Reduced crashes and error rates.</b></li>
        <li><b>Faster, more responsive user experience.</b></li>
        <li><b>Practical fixes that don't create new debt.</b></li>
      </ul>
    </p>
    <h3>Software Reliability & Scalability Improvements</h3>
    <p>
      As your product grows, reliability becomes as important as features. I
      help teams strengthen their systems so they can handle more users, more
      data, and more complexity without breaking. You gain confidence that your
      product can scale without hidden surprises.
    </p>
    <p>
      Typical outcomes:
      <ul>
        <li><b>Reduced operational risk for the team.</b></li>
        <li><b>Systems that stay up when traffic spikes.</b></li>
        <li><b>Cleaner architecture that supports growth.</b></li>
      </ul>
    </p>
    <h3>Release Engineering & Workflow Improvements</h3>
    <p>
      Shipping should feel smooth, not stressful. I work with teams to improve
      their build pipelines, release processes, and development workflows so
      they can move faster with less friction. The goal is simple: make it
      easier for your team to deliver great work without fighting the tools.
    </p>
    <p>
      Typical outcomes:
      <ul>
        <li><b>Faster, more reliable deployments.</b></li>
        <li><b>A calmer, more predictable release cycle.</b></li>
        <li><b>Clearer processes that unblock developers.</b></li>
      </ul>
    </p>
    <h3>Feature Development with Architectural Clarity</h3>
    <p>
      When you're shipping new features, you don't want to introduce complexity
      that slows you down later on. I help teams design and build features that
      fit cleanly into the existing system — or reshape it when needed. You get
      progress without the hidden cost.
    </p>
    <p>
      Typical outcomes:
      <ul>
        <li><b>Features that are maintainable from day one.</b></li>
        <li><b>Lower total cost of ownership for new functionality.</b></li>
        <li><b>A product that evolves without accumulating chaos.</b></li>
      </ul>
    </p>
    <h2>Who I Work With</h2>
    <p>
      I partner with teams who care about clarity, quality, and long‑term
      maintainability. Most of my clients fall into one of these groups:
      <ul>
        <li>
          <b>Product teams shipping complex applications.</b> Teams that need help
          diagnosing performance issues, improving reliability, or making architectural
          decisions with confidence.
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Early-stage startups.</b> Companies moving fast but starting to feel
          the weight of technical debt, unclear architecture, or slow delivery cycles.
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Engineering teams that want a trusted technical advisor.</b> Leads and
          founders who want a clear, experienced voice to help them make better technical
          decisions and avoid costly mistakes.
        </li>
      </ul>
      If your team values thoughtful engineering, clear communication, and practical
      solutions, we'll work well together.
    </p>
    <h2>How I Work</h2>
    <p>
      Working with me is straightforward and intentionally lightweight. My goal
      is to bring clarity, momentum, and technical confidence to your team
      without adding overhead or complexity.
      <ol>
        <li>
          <b>Fit Call.</b>
          A short conversation to understand your challenges, your goals, and whether
          I'm the right person to help. If I'm not, I'll point you in the right direction.
        </li><li>
          <b>Deep Dive.</b>
          If we're a match, we start with a focused outside-in exploration. I analyze
          the product experience and observability data alongside your codebase. This
          gives me the context I need to identify the real issues causing technical
          debt, system instability, or release delays.
        </li><li>
          <b>Engagement.</b>
          Depending on your needs, this can be weekly advisory, a targeted audit,
          or a short project. I work closely with your team, offering clear guidance,
          and practical solutions that fit your roadmap.
        </li><li>
          <b>Ongoing Support or Handoff.</b>
          Once the core work is done, I either stay on as a technical sounding board
          or hand everything off with clear next steps. The goal is always the same:
          leave your team stronger and more confident than before.
        </li>
      </ol>
      This process keeps things simple, predictable, and focused on outcomes.
    </p>
    <h2>Book a Fit Call</h2>
    <p>
      If this resonates, I'd love to learn more about what you're building.
      Let's have a short, friendly conversation where we explore your
      challenges, your goals, and whether I'm the right person to help. No
      pressure, no hard sell — just clarity.
    </p>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 items-start">
      <Button variant="primary" size="lg">Discuss your project</Button>
      <em>Book a fit call and we'll take it from there.</em>
    </div>
  </ServicePage>
</BaseLayout>
